            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0658" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12606: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-31T11:00:00+08:00">December 31, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>942. Legation’s 928, December 23, 4 p.m. The following telegram has been received
                    from Amoy: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 30, 4 p.m. Referring to my telegram of December 22, 5 p.m. As
                            precautionary measure all Americans at Changchow and <pb facs="0659"
                                n="557" xml:id="pg557"/> Siokhe have come to Amoy. All
                            communications unreliable and troops being sent northward. General
                            Gaston Wang has returned to Amoy. Local situation remains quiet but
                            tense.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
